{
  "schema": 1,
  "alert_over_pct": 10,
  "idle_frames": 125,
  "latency_budget_frames": 1,
  "notes": "125 frames * 16 ms = 2 s of the headless clock. strict_states must be fully quiet (no busy frame; presents only from a caret blink). Other states must be quiet at the end of the window: a one-shot Sub.at that fires and finishes still passes, a subscription still firing does not. The human --idle-check flag still requires settled() (quiet by the end and no re-wake). expect_busy records a state and does not fail; [\"*\"] exempts the example. scene3d subscribes every frame for the orbit and is exempt on purpose. gallery toasts and toast_sliding keep a tick subscription and are expect_busy. Latency budget is 1 frame (hit-test uses the previous frame). wasm_brotli_bytes is wasm32 ReleaseSmall, brotli quality 11, and is the portable budget. platforms.* native_exe_bytes, rss_bytes and committed_bytes are per host triple and GPU; 0 means unbudgeted and does not fail. The native exe is unstripped ReleaseSmall. committed_bytes is Committed_AS when the kernel prints it, else RssAnon+VmSwap. Fill a host triple with --update-budgets after a real run. x86_64 CI records native and RSS until that triple is filled in.",
